  "query_preview": "period of mild temperatures and dry conditions, fuels \nwill become drier with time and folks should continue to \nexercise caution near dry grasses, especially heading into \nmidweek with afternoon breeziness.\n\nThursday-weekend: Roughly 90% of the ensembles bring the \noffshore trough inland late in the week into the weekend. There \nare a myriad of outcomes with the exact timing, strength of the \nwave, and available moisture for precipitation. We can see this \nspread illustrated in the outcomes for high temperatures for \nThursday- Friday which could be as cool as mid 60s or warm as \nlower 80s. The cooling will bring an increase in winds with \nprobabilities indicating a 30-60% chance for wind gusts to be \nstronger than 20 mph. At this time, NBM carries the highest \nprobabilities on Friday. The incoming system will bring a chance\nfor light showers. Highest precipitation chances come in the \nmountains and lowest in the Basin. Depending how progressive or \nnon- progressive the system is will determine if any locations \nwill be capable of receiving a wetting rain (0.10\"). \nProbabilities at this time top out between 20-30% mainly \nfavoring the Cascade Crest and Selkirk's across NE WA and N \nIdaho. /sb",
